# .geminiignore -- agent file visibility for Gemini CLI tools
# (ReadFile / Glob / SearchText / ReadFolder)
#
# THIS IS A SELF-CONTAINED DENYLIST (rewritten 2026-06-07; supersedes BUG-018 attempt).
#
# Why the old version was broken:
#   Gemini's native file tools previously honored BOTH .gitignore and this file.
#   .gitignore has a blanket directory rule `workspaces/**/interns/`. A gitignore
#   DIRECTORY exclusion cannot be undone by a child `!negation` (git never descends
#   into an ignored dir), so the old `!.../interns/reports/**/*.md` re-includes here
#   were inert. Read-only subagents (the built-in `generalist`) therefore got
#   "ignored by configured ignore patterns" and could not read any interns/ artifact.
#
# The fix:
#   .gemini/settings.json now sets fileFiltering.respectGitIgnore=false and
#   respectGeminiIgnore=true. So this file is the ONLY visibility filter for agents
#   and MUST positively hide everything sensitive/heavy on its own. git commit
#   behavior is UNCHANGED (git still ignores interns/ via .gitignore).
#
#   The lightweight interns/ artifacts (reports/**, generated/**, current.json|md,
#   handoffs/*.md, metadata_store/**) are intentionally NOT listed below, so native
#   ReadFile/Glob can reach them.
#
# MAINTENANCE RULE: because git's denylist no longer protects agent visibility, any
# NEW secret/PHI/heavy path must be added here explicitly.

# -- secrets (NEVER expose to an agent) --------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.databrickscfg
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
credentials*
config/lock.toml
!config/lock.toml.example

# -- raw source data (may contain PHI) ---------------------------------------
workspaces/**/datasets/

# -- heavy / noisy machine artifacts (token discipline) ----------------------
#    full session logs, tool-call traces, and raw Delta/medallion data
workspaces/**/interns/state/**/session.json
workspaces/**/interns/state/**/*trajectory*
workspaces/**/interns/state/**/medallion/
state/
.agents/sessions/
*.duckdb
*.db
*.sqlite
*.log

# -- caches / build / vcs (performance) --------------------------------------
.git/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.idea/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
node_modules/
dist/
build/
